<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Demerara-Essequibo</h1><p class="st-meta">1812 CE – 1831 CE · capital Georgetown</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A British-ruled sugar colony on the Guiana coast, formed from two Dutch colonies and shaken by the great slave rebellion of 1823.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> had occupied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colonies of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/demerara">Demerara</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/essequibo">Essequibo</a> in 1796 and, after their brief return to the Dutch in 1802, again from 1803. In 1812 the British administration united them as Demerara-Essequibo, renaming the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgetown-guyana">Stabroek</a> as Georgetown, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-dutch-treaty-of-1814">Convention of London</a> in 1814 formally ceded the territory to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The colony kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> laws and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/court-of-policy">Court of Policy</a>, in which planters held most power. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">Sugar</a> dominated the economy, worked by tens of thousands of enslaved Africans. In August 1823 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/demerara">Demerara</a> rebellion involved some 10,000 or more enslaved people, who demanded rights they believed had been granted in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>. It was crushed with many executions. The missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-smith-missionary">John Smith</a>, accused of encouraging it, died in prison, inspiring abolitionists in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1831 Demerara-Essequibo was merged with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/berbice">Berbice</a> to form <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-guiana">British Guiana</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">Slavery</a> was abolished across the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a> in 1834. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgetown-guyana">Georgetown</a> remained the capital and is today the capital of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/co-operative-republic-of-guyana">Guyana</a>, and the rebellion of 1823 is remembered as a milestone on the road to emancipation.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/demerara-essequibo.jpg" alt="Demerara-Essequibo" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Original: Acts of Union 1800 Vector: Yaddah · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_(3-5).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1812 CE – 1831 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Georgetown</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>John Murray</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/guyana">Guyana</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>United Colony of Demerara and Essequibo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1822&amp;focus=demerara-essequibo" aria-label="Demerara-Essequibo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3070 1923 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Demerara-Essequibo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3390 2179L3380 2180M3390 2179L3390 2179M3390 2179L4997 651M3390 2179L3390 2179"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3380 2180h0M3390 2179h0M4997 651h0M3390 2179h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3390 2179h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3390 2179h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1